01:04:10,000 --> 01:04:16,000
Every Which Way but Loose is a 1978 American action
comedy film released by Warner Bros.

15
01:08:45,000 --> 01:08:51,000
starring Clint Eastwood in an uncharacteristic and offbeat comedy role.

16
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
It was produced by Robert Daley and directed by James Fargo.

17
01:17:55,000 --> 01:18:01,000
Eastwood plays Philo Beddoe, a trucker and bare-knuckle brawler roaming the American West in search of a
lost love while accompanied by his brother/manager Orville and his pet orangutan Clyde.

18
01:22:30,000 --> 01:22:36,000
Philo encounters a wide assortment of characters, including a pair of police
officers and a motorcycle gang who pursue him for revenge.

19
01:27:05,000 --> 01:27:11,000
Eastwood's appearance in the film, after his string of Spaghetti Western and Dirty Harry roles,
somewhat startled the film industry, and he was reportedly advised against taking the role.

20
01:31:40,000 --> 01:31:46,000
Although it was poorly reviewed by critics, the film proved successful and became, along with its
1980 sequel Any Which Way You Can, two of the highest-grossing Eastwood films.

21
01:36:15,000 --> 01:36:21,000
When adjusted for inflation, it ranks as one of the top
250 highest-grossing films of all time.

